WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.715
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.985 --> 00:03.025
-There's still time to withdraw. -Yeah.

3
00:03.105 --> 00:04.945
If you don't have a band, you can't compete.

4
00:05.025 --> 00:07.705
Do you think anyone will actually apply?

5
00:07.785 --> 00:10.185
If we can't find applicants ourselves, we'll have to rely on the universe.

6
00:10.265 --> 00:12.545
"A moonlight-bathing ritual to ward off bad luck."

7
00:12.625 --> 00:14.745
-You want me to get naked? -I think you should try it.

8
00:14.825 --> 00:17.705
-How about this? You jump, I jump. Deal? -Huh?

9
00:17.785 --> 00:20.505
May the moonlight shining down tonight

10
00:20.585 --> 00:23.385
cleanse Khobfa of every bit of bad luck.

11
00:23.465 --> 00:27.105
And please let the person standing in front of me become my boyfriend.

12
00:31.105 --> 00:32.625
Hello, everyone.

13
00:32.705 --> 00:36.185
Right now, our band is looking for just three more members.

14
00:36.265 --> 00:41.185
If you're interested in joining Horizon, come meet us in the audition room.

15
00:41.785 --> 00:44.185
Anyone thinking of joining this band should think twice.

16
00:44.905 --> 00:47.385
The reason no one wants to join is that…

17
00:47.465 --> 00:49.225
Never mind.

18
00:49.305 --> 00:51.705
What made you even want to enter a band competition?

19
00:52.265 --> 00:53.465
Hang in there.

20
00:53.545 --> 00:55.785
It must be exhausting to try this hard.

21
00:56.385 --> 00:59.265
If you can't say anything nice, then don't say anything at all. Got it?

22
00:59.345 --> 01:01.305
What the hell is wrong with you all?

23
01:01.385 --> 01:03.545
-You-- -Hey, calm down. Don't insult them.

24
01:03.625 --> 01:06.705
If you're interested in the audition, see you later today.

25
01:06.785 --> 01:09.305
-Damn! -Relax.

26
01:12.945 --> 01:14.425
You've got talent.

27
01:15.545 --> 01:19.465
I want them to see it and shut up already.

28
01:32.785 --> 01:34.025
Smile a little.

29
01:34.105 --> 01:38.305
No one wants to join a band with someone who's always frowning. Trust me.

30
01:46.905 --> 01:49.825
What? Why did you come close?

31
01:58.945 --> 02:00.625
Why isn't anyone coming?

32
02:01.865 --> 02:03.385
I told you.

33
02:03.465 --> 02:06.505
You look too grumpy. No one wants to be in a band with you.

34
02:09.864 --> 02:10.864
What?

35
02:10.945 --> 02:12.945
Ohm! Jinnie!

36
02:13.945 --> 02:15.705
Holy shit, it actually worked.

37
02:17.185 --> 02:19.585
Friends don't abandon each other.

38
02:20.185 --> 02:22.345
Come on, Rin, Khobfa.

39
02:22.425 --> 02:23.785
Let's chase our dreams.

40
02:26.185 --> 02:29.265
Hey, aren't we still one member short?

41
02:33.105 --> 02:36.745
If Ohm and Jinnie are joining us, then we only have one choice left.

42
03:40.025 --> 03:41.665
THE GRANDEST CONTEST OF OUR UNIVERSITY

43
03:41.745 --> 03:43.505
AUDITION REGISTRATION

44
03:48.785 --> 03:50.665
Have Rin and Khobfa signed up yet?

45
03:50.745 --> 03:51.905
Not yet.

46
03:55.385 --> 03:58.705
-Maybe they couldn't find enough members. -How do you know we couldn't?

47
04:07.225 --> 04:08.425
You're one person short.

48
04:09.745 --> 04:11.145
Rin.

49
04:11.225 --> 04:12.745
You told him already, right?

50
04:13.945 --> 04:16.504
Yeah, I did. He said yes.

51
04:17.105 --> 04:18.705
Then why isn't he here yet?

52
04:22.265 --> 04:24.465
Where's your last member?

53
04:31.505 --> 04:32.585
I'm here.

54
04:33.305 --> 04:35.585
I'm sorry. I got a little lost.

55
04:35.665 --> 04:37.305
Danthai, come here quickly.

56
04:43.145 --> 04:45.825
It's not 4 p.m. yet. We can still sign up, right?

57
04:45.905 --> 04:47.105
Go ahead.

58
04:51.745 --> 04:53.465
These guys are your bandmates?

59
04:54.185 --> 04:55.265
Can they even play instruments?

60
05:00.545 --> 05:01.705
Of course they can.

61
05:02.865 --> 05:04.585
Why else would we be signing up?

62
05:06.185 --> 05:07.105
Right, guys?

63
05:07.185 --> 05:09.625
-Yeah. -Yeah.

64
05:10.585 --> 05:11.985
I'm so good at it.

65
05:24.745 --> 05:26.065
I can only play the melodica.

66
05:26.145 --> 05:27.625
I've only played drums at Sports Day.

67
05:27.705 --> 05:28.865
I've only played the tingnong.

68
05:29.945 --> 05:31.105
Shit.

69
05:31.185 --> 05:34.025
If I'd known from the start, I wouldn't have entered.

70
05:34.105 --> 05:37.665
Hey, come on. Give it a try.

71
05:37.745 --> 05:40.945
We have five days before the first round.

72
05:41.905 --> 05:46.025
We have to make it into the final five bands.

73
05:46.105 --> 05:47.625
-We can do it! -We can do it!

74
06:01.105 --> 06:02.225
My dream!

75
06:02.305 --> 06:07.625
No way!

76
06:23.025 --> 06:24.105
I'll take this one.

77
06:24.185 --> 06:25.985
Sure. This model is really good.

78
06:26.065 --> 06:27.225
I highly recommend it.

79
06:27.945 --> 06:30.025
-I'll get it ready for you. -Here.

80
06:32.825 --> 06:34.185
How would you like to pay?

81
06:34.265 --> 06:35.465
Here you are. My credit card.

82
06:36.025 --> 06:38.145
Sure. Please wait a moment.

83
06:43.345 --> 06:45.825
You're like a dog with a new toy.

84
06:46.465 --> 06:49.225
Are you going to sleep hugging that guitar tonight?

85
06:49.305 --> 06:50.185
No.

86
06:50.945 --> 06:52.545
I'd rather hug you.

87
06:54.385 --> 06:56.905
You look cool when you hold a guitar.

88
06:59.625 --> 07:01.545
Sir, I'm sorry.

89
07:01.625 --> 07:03.625
Would another payment method work for you?

90
07:03.705 --> 07:05.745
Your credit card was declined.

91
07:09.105 --> 07:10.425
I'm really sorry.

92
07:12.425 --> 07:15.225
Maybe next time, then.

93
07:18.825 --> 07:20.065
We'll come back later.

94
07:20.145 --> 07:21.465
I'm really sorry.

95
07:26.585 --> 07:31.345
Hello? I'm trying to buy something, but my credit card isn't working.

96
07:31.425 --> 07:32.505
Is something wrong?

97
07:33.105 --> 07:37.185
Krit, your dad had your credit card canceled.

98
07:37.265 --> 07:40.425
He said it'll stay that way until you learn what's right and wrong.

99
07:40.505 --> 07:42.145
Do you have enough money, dear?

100
07:42.225 --> 07:45.345
It's okay. I'll manage. Don't worry, Mom.

101
07:54.945 --> 07:56.105
What happened?

102
07:56.905 --> 07:58.345
I don't think I want to compete anymore.

103
07:58.945 --> 08:00.025
What? Why?

104
08:01.825 --> 08:03.145
I don't want to do this anymore.

105
08:03.745 --> 08:05.465
I think I should stop.

106
08:27.745 --> 08:30.105
Do you think you can teach them to get better in time?

107
08:31.345 --> 08:33.225
-No. -Huh?

108
08:33.825 --> 08:36.345
Your friends might not improve overnight,

109
08:36.425 --> 08:40.425
but our band members never back down.

110
08:40.505 --> 08:42.065
No wonder they're your friends.

111
08:42.664 --> 08:43.985
They're your friends too.

112
08:48.265 --> 08:49.785
You're our friend.

113
08:50.465 --> 08:52.425
Whenever you do something you love,

114
08:52.505 --> 08:55.385
no matter how hard it is, you always give it your all.

115
08:56.825 --> 08:58.025
What's with you?

116
08:58.105 --> 09:00.385
Why are you suddenly giving me a confidence booster?

117
09:00.465 --> 09:03.385
Come on. Help me pick a song.

118
09:05.785 --> 09:08.545
What are the options?

119
09:23.505 --> 09:24.505
Is this one good?

120
09:25.105 --> 09:28.145
It's not bad, but do you have anything else?

121
09:29.425 --> 09:30.345
Wait a second.

122
09:30.865 --> 09:33.145
I've listened to this one before.

123
09:33.225 --> 09:34.985
-This one? -Yeah.

124
09:35.065 --> 09:36.345
How about this one?

125
09:38.065 --> 09:39.545
Wait.

126
09:40.145 --> 09:41.505
Try this one.

127
09:42.105 --> 09:43.025
Okay.

128
09:45.985 --> 09:51.745
Only you can stop my heart right here

129
09:51.825 --> 09:56.385
Where you are

130
09:57.785 --> 10:02.145
You're the only one I want

131
10:02.225 --> 10:07.665
With all my soul and heart

132
10:07.745 --> 10:10.705
I'll find every way to love you

133
10:10.785 --> 10:14.385
No matter when or where

134
10:14.465 --> 10:19.545
My whole heart belongs to you alone

135
10:21.865 --> 10:23.745
Why did you bring me here again?

136
10:24.825 --> 10:26.105
I told you I was done.

137
10:37.145 --> 10:38.225
Mochi.

138
10:40.225 --> 10:41.305
You…

139
10:44.145 --> 10:45.825
I'm not giving it to you for free.

140
10:45.905 --> 10:48.545
Win the prize money, then pay me back.

141
10:49.865 --> 10:51.505
Can I really do this?

142
10:52.505 --> 10:55.065
Even my family doesn't believe in me.

143
10:57.345 --> 10:58.585
Then look over there.

144
11:10.425 --> 11:12.705
I'm waiting to see you on stage, Krit!

145
11:12.785 --> 11:14.825
Fighting, Krit.

146
11:14.905 --> 11:17.585
I'm waiting for your performance.

147
11:23.825 --> 11:25.945
Even if your family doesn't support you,

148
11:26.665 --> 11:29.025
you've gotten yourself this far.

149
11:30.145 --> 11:31.105
Look.

150
11:32.065 --> 11:34.065
So many fans are here to support you.

151
11:34.745 --> 11:38.105
And you've got me cheering you on.

152
11:42.945 --> 11:44.585
Are you really not going to keep fighting?

153
11:47.265 --> 11:50.665
Show your dad how good you are.

154
12:05.625 --> 12:07.105
I'm sorry, bro.

155
12:07.185 --> 12:10.105
The professor let us out a little late. Are we still doing this?

156
12:17.825 --> 12:19.905
Come on. Let's win this!

157
12:21.985 --> 12:22.825
The Winner!

158
13:10.585 --> 13:11.745
Guys, look.

159
13:11.825 --> 13:15.385
The competition hasn't even started, yet they've already won over all the fans.

160
13:15.945 --> 13:19.345
Seriously. Their teamwork is insanely good.

161
13:19.425 --> 13:21.865
Wow, Krit is amazing.

162
13:21.945 --> 13:23.185
Dan!

163
13:24.065 --> 13:25.265
Go!

164
13:27.185 --> 13:28.065
I'm sorry.

165
13:28.145 --> 13:30.785
I thought someone like me, who only played drums on Sports Day,

166
13:30.865 --> 13:34.425
could never compete with them.

167
13:45.585 --> 13:46.705
I just thought of something.

168
13:47.305 --> 13:48.985
I want to try something.

169
13:52.865 --> 13:54.985
You guys brought your things, right?

170
13:56.825 --> 13:57.985
-Yeah. -Yeah.

171
14:08.345 --> 14:11.465
Are these lucky team shirts really going to work?

172
14:13.825 --> 14:15.025
I don't know,

173
14:15.105 --> 14:17.385
but we have to try everything now.

174
14:20.825 --> 14:22.785
GOOD LUCK

175
14:22.865 --> 14:24.065
Try it on.

176
14:27.585 --> 14:28.425
Here.

177
14:36.225 --> 14:38.145
Well? Do I look handsome?

178
14:38.225 --> 14:41.025
Oh, you look handsome. Super handsome.

179
14:41.105 --> 14:43.385
No one can compare to you. I've never seen anyone so handsome.

180
14:43.465 --> 14:45.705
You look like you've never done anything wrong in your life.

181
14:45.785 --> 14:48.585
You're exaggerating. Go put yours on too.

182
14:59.905 --> 15:01.985
-Here. -Hold this for me.

183
15:08.065 --> 15:10.345
Oh, whoa!

184
15:10.425 --> 15:11.305
VICTORY

185
15:11.385 --> 15:14.825
"Good luck," "Victory," "nine-nine."

186
15:16.545 --> 15:20.705
All these auspicious words will definitely bring our team good fortune.

187
15:20.785 --> 15:22.705
We'll easily pass the first round.

188
15:24.265 --> 15:26.665
My boyfriend really knows how to fill me with positivity.

189
15:26.745 --> 15:30.225
Huh? Boyfriend? Nonsense.

190
15:30.305 --> 15:31.985
Focus on the competition.

191
15:32.065 --> 15:34.705
If I win, will you be my boyfriend?

192
15:39.585 --> 15:43.825
You're so obsessed with this, huh? Get through the first round first.

193
15:50.225 --> 15:51.225
Move.

194
16:01.305 --> 16:06.225
Because someone unnecessary Has to walk away

195
16:06.305 --> 16:10.825
No matter how much I love you inside

196
16:10.905 --> 16:15.185
Someone unnecessary shouldn't be here

197
16:15.265 --> 16:20.305
I understand that you don't need me

198
16:20.385 --> 16:26.825
I'll leave in tears as someone worthless

199
16:26.905 --> 16:32.185
Because it's a necessity Of someone unnecessary

200
16:41.065 --> 16:46.345
Because it's a necessity Of someone unnecessary

201
16:51.465 --> 16:54.625
This is the Winner!

202
16:54.705 --> 16:57.345
Let's give them another round of applause!

203
16:59.025 --> 17:03.145
And here are the band manager and members.

204
17:03.225 --> 17:05.385
Damn. He's so good.

205
17:05.464 --> 17:06.865
That's so cool.

206
17:08.385 --> 17:09.665
We can also do it.

207
17:10.265 --> 17:11.464
We can do it.

208
17:11.545 --> 17:16.745
And our next band, please welcome Horizon!

209
17:20.265 --> 17:23.865
You have 15 minutes to prepare.

210
17:23.944 --> 17:26.704
Please come onstage and get ready.

211
17:41.065 --> 17:42.585
We can do this, guys!

212
17:42.665 --> 17:43.505
We can!

213
17:44.465 --> 17:46.745
-Horizon, fight! -Fight!

214
17:56.665 --> 17:58.025
This will really work, right?

215
17:59.465 --> 18:00.385
Good question.

216
18:39.985 --> 18:45.625
You are everything In my reality and dreams

217
18:45.705 --> 18:50.305
You are everything My heart could ever want

218
18:50.385 --> 18:57.305
You are the story I read Before I close my eyes and dream

219
18:57.945 --> 19:02.385
Don't tell me you're making us play these main instruments too.

220
19:02.465 --> 19:03.505
Yeah.

221
19:04.505 --> 19:06.505
Since we're doing a cover anyway,

222
19:07.225 --> 19:10.105
we just have to put our own identity into the song.

223
19:11.665 --> 19:13.785
Friends don't abandon each other.

224
19:13.865 --> 19:15.665
Come on, Rin, Khobfa.

225
19:15.745 --> 19:17.185
Let's chase our dreams.

226
19:20.385 --> 19:23.465
Our band members never give up.

227
19:23.545 --> 19:25.385
No wonder they're your friends.

228
19:25.465 --> 19:27.265
They're your friends too.

229
19:27.345 --> 19:28.905
You're our friend.

230
19:30.985 --> 19:34.545
Right where you are

231
19:36.345 --> 19:40.785
You're the only one I want

232
19:40.865 --> 19:45.265
With all my soul and heart

233
19:45.345 --> 19:51.065
I'll find every way to love you No matter when or where

234
19:51.145 --> 19:56.505
My whole heart belongs to you alone

235
20:14.305 --> 20:19.545
Next, we will announce the bands selected for the finals

236
20:19.625 --> 20:22.625
of the Campus Stage competition.

237
20:22.705 --> 20:26.265
Only five bands will advance to the final round.

238
20:26.345 --> 20:30.265
The first selected band is…

239
20:34.665 --> 20:36.625
The Winner!

240
20:45.825 --> 20:48.145
Moving on to the next band…

241
20:48.825 --> 20:52.065
The next band is…

242
20:53.745 --> 20:55.545
Stand Still!

243
20:55.625 --> 20:57.185
-Yeah! -Yeah!

244
21:01.505 --> 21:05.625
And the next band is…

245
21:05.705 --> 21:07.585
Friends with Deadlines!

246
21:11.865 --> 21:14.625
There are only two spots left.

247
21:16.025 --> 21:20.265
The next band advancing is…

248
21:24.225 --> 21:26.225
-Sakit! -Yeah!

249
21:28.545 --> 21:30.305
And now, for the final band.

250
21:30.905 --> 21:34.945
This band received points for their creativity.

251
21:35.025 --> 21:41.065
Although their performance wasn't perfect, the judges saw their determination.

252
21:41.145 --> 21:46.505
The final band advancing to the next round is…

253
21:54.585 --> 21:57.505
Horizon!

254
21:57.585 --> 21:59.225
We made it!

255
22:01.305 --> 22:03.025
-Let's go! -Come on!

256
22:03.105 --> 22:05.705
Congratulations!

257
22:07.425 --> 22:09.505
I told you my shirts work, didn't I?

258
22:09.585 --> 22:12.905
They say "Good luck" and "Victory."

259
22:13.505 --> 22:15.425
So we got "Lucky."

260
22:15.505 --> 22:17.625
Lucky. Why?

261
22:17.705 --> 22:18.625
Yeah.

262
22:26.665 --> 22:31.145
Congratulations again to all five bands advancing.

263
22:37.145 --> 22:38.585
Over the next two weeks,

264
22:38.665 --> 22:42.945
you must prepare a song for the championship round.

265
22:43.025 --> 22:45.505
Guys, we only have two weeks?

266
22:46.905 --> 22:47.985
We can do it.

267
22:48.785 --> 22:52.625
The rule is that every band must perform one song.

268
22:52.705 --> 22:57.745
You may rearrange an existing song or write an original song.

269
22:57.825 --> 23:01.945
However, bands that write an original song

270
23:02.025 --> 23:07.665
will receive bonus points from our judges for originality.

271
23:07.745 --> 23:09.225
Bonus points?

272
23:11.345 --> 23:13.505
Which option will each band choose?

273
23:13.585 --> 23:15.265
Please decide by today.

274
23:15.945 --> 23:18.545
You have ten minutes to discuss.

275
23:19.265 --> 23:20.305
You may begin.

276
23:24.505 --> 23:26.185
Writing a new song sounds interesting,

277
23:26.265 --> 23:28.745
but two weeks is too little time.

278
23:29.345 --> 23:32.465
We'd have to write the lyrics and melody,

279
23:33.545 --> 23:35.345
then practice until we can play it well.

280
23:35.425 --> 23:36.825
I think it's too risky.

281
23:36.905 --> 23:37.825
True.

282
23:37.905 --> 23:39.585
I agree.

283
23:39.665 --> 23:43.105
If the new song turns out badly, our total score will plummet.

284
23:43.185 --> 23:46.505
Let's take a song people already know and make it cool in our own style.

285
23:47.065 --> 23:48.745
-It'd be safer. -Yeah.

286
23:49.905 --> 23:50.945
I agree.

287
23:51.825 --> 23:54.065
Khobfa, let's write a new song.

288
23:54.145 --> 23:55.625
There will be bonus points.

289
23:58.265 --> 23:59.745
Look at our band members.

290
23:59.825 --> 24:01.705
It won't be easy, Rin.

291
24:01.785 --> 24:03.625
Should we really play it safe?

292
24:03.705 --> 24:05.785
Look at that band.

293
24:05.865 --> 24:07.545
They're scary as hell.

294
24:13.025 --> 24:14.065
What do you think, Khobfa?

295
24:15.065 --> 24:16.345
It's up to you.

296
24:16.425 --> 24:18.145
Whatever you say, I'm in.

297
24:22.825 --> 24:24.625
Time's up.

298
24:25.225 --> 24:27.185
Please turn around.

299
24:30.945 --> 24:34.025
Which bands will rearrange an existing song?

300
24:34.625 --> 24:36.785
Please have one representative raise their hand.

301
24:47.185 --> 24:51.225
What about Horizon?

302
25:03.065 --> 25:04.505
Horizon will write an original song.

303
25:14.465 --> 25:16.705
Statistically, no band has ever won

304
25:16.785 --> 25:19.265
with an original song in the past four years.

305
25:19.345 --> 25:21.385
Isn't Khobfa taking too big a risk?

306
25:33.905 --> 25:35.865
Mark Zuckerberg once said,

307
25:37.025 --> 25:40.345
"The biggest risk is not taking one."

308
25:41.385 --> 25:43.305
If we keep doing the same thing,

309
25:43.385 --> 25:45.305
our chances of winning are slim.

310
25:45.385 --> 25:48.705
But if we take the risk, we still have a chance.

311
25:48.785 --> 25:50.025
Let's go for it.

312
25:50.105 --> 25:52.585
We have nothing to lose.

313
25:52.665 --> 25:55.625
You're right. Let's do this.

314
25:56.225 --> 26:00.745
Khobfa, since you said all that, do you already have an idea?

315
26:00.825 --> 26:02.265
-Not yet. -What?

316
26:03.865 --> 26:08.025
That's why I called you guys to brainstorm.

317
26:09.105 --> 26:10.665
But I have one thing in mind.

318
26:10.745 --> 26:12.265
It has to be about love.

319
26:12.345 --> 26:13.665
-Love? -Love?

320
26:13.745 --> 26:15.945
That's way too broad, man.

321
26:16.585 --> 26:18.585
Can you narrow it down?

322
26:19.785 --> 26:24.585
Hey, what if it's about memories of love?

323
26:24.665 --> 26:26.545
-Yeah. -Yeah.

324
26:26.625 --> 26:27.985
That sounds interesting.

325
26:28.065 --> 26:29.065
How about this?

326
26:29.145 --> 26:32.345
We'll take turns sharing our memories of love,

327
26:32.425 --> 26:35.265
then vote on which one is best.

328
26:35.865 --> 26:36.825
-Sounds good? -Yeah.

329
26:36.905 --> 26:37.945
Okay.

330
26:38.025 --> 26:40.025
Who wants to start?

331
26:40.105 --> 26:41.865
Me. I'll go first.

332
26:46.425 --> 26:49.825
I've had a crush on someone for a long time.

333
26:50.665 --> 26:52.665
I talk to him every day,

334
26:52.745 --> 26:54.425
but what should I do?

335
26:55.345 --> 26:56.865
It seems like he likes me,

336
26:57.425 --> 26:58.945
but he won't make it clear.

337
26:59.025 --> 27:00.665
Sorry, Jinnie.

338
27:00.745 --> 27:02.345
You have someone you're talking to?

339
27:02.425 --> 27:05.665
Come on. It's Baron.

340
27:07.225 --> 27:08.905
He's AI.

341
27:08.985 --> 27:10.425
-What? -What?

342
27:11.545 --> 27:13.625
I talk to him day and night.

343
27:14.705 --> 27:18.785
How do I get him to be my boyfriend already?

344
27:18.865 --> 27:22.025
Oh, Jinnie. That's enough.

345
27:22.105 --> 27:23.265
Sit down.

346
27:23.345 --> 27:24.745
Let's hear my story instead.

347
27:26.985 --> 27:29.065
Fluke and I.

348
27:30.545 --> 27:32.985
My love story with Fluke.

349
27:34.145 --> 27:35.265
What faculty is he in?

350
27:35.345 --> 27:37.225
How could I not know about this one?

351
27:37.825 --> 27:39.225
I don't know either.

352
27:39.305 --> 27:42.305
We met through DMs.

353
27:42.385 --> 27:45.305
He messaged me first, so we exchanged numbers.

354
27:46.025 --> 27:49.185
He called me day and night.

355
27:49.265 --> 27:53.825
But whenever he had a problem, I had to send him money to help.

356
27:53.905 --> 27:56.065
For phone credit and rent.

357
27:56.145 --> 28:00.585
There were a lot of problems later on, so my bank account ran dry.

358
28:00.665 --> 28:01.865
You idiot.

359
28:02.425 --> 28:03.345
Hey.

360
28:03.985 --> 28:05.545
That's called a scammer.

361
28:05.625 --> 28:07.865
-A scammer? -How did you fall for that?

362
28:07.945 --> 28:10.065
You fell for an AI!

363
28:10.145 --> 28:13.985
Enough, you two. Sit down.

364
28:19.745 --> 28:23.305
Dan, you're our last hope.

365
28:23.385 --> 28:25.345
I hope your story is useful.

366
28:25.425 --> 28:26.905
It should be.

367
28:27.665 --> 28:30.905
But it's a little painful.

368
28:31.505 --> 28:32.505
-What? -Oh, hey.

369
28:33.305 --> 28:36.865
Damn. This sounds promising.

370
28:38.345 --> 28:40.145
I fell in love with a rice shop vendor.

371
28:40.225 --> 28:41.545
-What? -What?

372
28:41.625 --> 28:46.665
Why? Love these days has no definition.

373
28:47.265 --> 28:48.585
Hold on, Dan.

374
28:48.665 --> 28:50.825
How did you fall for her?

375
28:51.785 --> 28:54.025
She called me handsome.

376
28:55.865 --> 28:58.705
Every time I went to her shop, she would call me handsome.

377
28:58.785 --> 29:00.985
She even asked me to order an extra size.

378
29:01.065 --> 29:04.305
Then one day, I found out the truth.

379
29:06.745 --> 29:07.705
What?

380
29:09.145 --> 29:12.505
She calls every man who comes in "handsome."

381
29:12.585 --> 29:13.745
Damn.

382
29:14.265 --> 29:18.265
You can't play with someone's heart like that.

383
29:21.305 --> 29:25.105
Dan, there are plenty of rice shop vendors out there.

384
29:25.185 --> 29:26.065
Okay?

385
29:26.745 --> 29:30.305
Danthai, don't cry.

386
29:31.025 --> 29:32.505
You'll make me cry too.

387
29:38.945 --> 29:40.505
No, hold the ends.

388
29:40.585 --> 29:41.865
Hold the ends.

389
29:42.785 --> 29:43.945
What's the problem?

390
29:44.025 --> 29:46.785
The strings are thick. My fingers hurt.

391
29:47.785 --> 29:49.025
Press harder. Press.

392
29:49.105 --> 29:50.145
Let me see.

393
29:50.225 --> 29:52.225
You already have some experience, right?

394
29:57.905 --> 29:58.745
I see.

395
29:58.825 --> 29:59.785
Keep practicing.

396
29:59.865 --> 30:01.105
You're actually not bad.

397
30:20.265 --> 30:22.385
If we hadn't talked to them,

398
30:22.465 --> 30:25.465
we would never have known they had such strange love stories.

399
30:27.945 --> 30:29.145
Are they strange?

400
30:29.745 --> 30:32.305
I still think they're love stories.

401
30:33.225 --> 30:37.505
Do you have a love story you want to share with me?

402
30:39.425 --> 30:44.025
It's probably the time I got to spend with you.

403
30:47.425 --> 30:48.545
Khobfa.

404
30:50.265 --> 30:53.425
If you knew I was the one who's been making you unlucky,

405
30:53.505 --> 30:55.465
would you still love me?

406
30:58.305 --> 30:59.425
Why did you hide it from me?

407
30:59.505 --> 31:02.025
A presto amora!

408
31:02.105 --> 31:05.825
If you choose to inherit it, you must prepare to be unlucky in love.

409
31:05.905 --> 31:09.465
-Khobfa! -I regret ever trusting you.

410
31:09.545 --> 31:10.745
Rin?

411
31:10.825 --> 31:11.905
Rin.

412
31:13.345 --> 31:15.945
What's with you? You've been thinking for so long.

413
31:17.305 --> 31:19.225
Do you have anything to share?

414
31:21.185 --> 31:24.825
It's probably the time I got to spend with you.

415
31:27.745 --> 31:28.985
Same here.

416
31:29.585 --> 31:34.145
You made my time so meaningful.

417
31:39.345 --> 31:43.825
You're always in my business, and you're a drunk too.

418
31:43.905 --> 31:46.145
I have to get you a ride home every day.

419
31:46.225 --> 31:48.785
Wait. Are you insulting me?

420
31:48.865 --> 31:50.025
No.

421
31:55.745 --> 31:59.505
Honestly, you've always supported me.

422
31:59.585 --> 32:01.305
Without you,

423
32:02.265 --> 32:04.825
I never thought I could come this far.

424
32:06.985 --> 32:10.825
Thank you, really, for coming into my life.

425
32:33.665 --> 32:34.985
Rin.

426
32:36.145 --> 32:38.705
I left the report due this evening in my room.

427
32:39.305 --> 32:42.225
Can you get it for me? I haven't finished practicing yet.

428
32:42.305 --> 32:45.945
Okay. You keep practicing. I'll get it.

429
32:46.545 --> 32:47.545
It's your old room.

430
32:47.625 --> 32:49.505
I already claimed it from you.

431
32:49.585 --> 32:50.545
Yeah.

432
32:50.625 --> 32:52.425
Wait.

433
32:52.505 --> 32:54.985
Hasn't the owner asked for the house back?

434
32:59.065 --> 33:02.105
Dan's mom owns the house.

435
33:02.185 --> 33:04.065
She is the owner.

436
33:04.145 --> 33:07.305
-Right, Dan? -Yeah. She's renovating it to sell.

437
33:09.385 --> 33:10.705
I'm off.

438
33:14.585 --> 33:16.425
I'll get back to practicing, then.

439
33:30.025 --> 33:32.025
Damn. My room!

440
33:33.865 --> 33:36.585
Gosh. It's such a mess.

441
33:40.545 --> 33:41.865
Where is it?

442
33:44.585 --> 33:46.705
Dan didn't tell me.

443
34:04.625 --> 34:09.545
Oh shit! This is the missing page from the owl spellbook.

444
34:23.105 --> 34:26.105
THE CURSED PERSON WILL LOSE ALL MEMORIES OF THE CURSER

445
34:26.824 --> 34:30.665
Why is the cure for the curse here?

446
34:40.945 --> 34:42.625
To lift the curse,

447
34:42.705 --> 34:47.824
the curser must take the item used for it, make a wish, and recite

448
34:47.905 --> 34:50.145
"finito amora."

449
34:50.225 --> 34:53.304
However, once the curse is lifted,

450
34:53.385 --> 34:57.385
the cursed person will lose all memories of the curser,

451
34:57.465 --> 34:59.585
as if they never knew each other.

452
35:00.185 --> 35:06.345
"The cursed person will lose all memories of the curser."

453
35:21.585 --> 35:23.545
I found a way to lift the curse, guys.

454
35:26.185 --> 35:28.105
Congratulations, Rin.

455
35:28.185 --> 35:29.505
Do it quickly.

456
35:29.585 --> 35:31.825
The spirits have opened the way.

457
35:31.905 --> 35:37.105
If you don't do it now, something worse might happen.

458
35:46.105 --> 35:49.505
THE CURSER MUST TAKE THE ITEM USED FOR IT, MAKE A WISH, AND RECITE "FINITO AMORA."

459
35:49.585 --> 35:50.905
HOWEVER, ONCE THE CURSE IS LIFTED,

460
35:50.985 --> 35:52.705
THE CURSED PERSON WILL LOSE ALL MEMORIES OF THE CURSER

461
36:08.225 --> 36:10.905
Yet there is one lucky thing.

462
36:11.745 --> 36:14.465
Whatever happens, you are always there.

463
36:15.145 --> 36:17.745
Your birthday is on the final day.

464
36:18.345 --> 36:21.105
I want us to share a memory that day.

465
36:50.505 --> 36:51.465
Hey.

466
36:54.065 --> 36:56.345
Congratulations on passing the first round.

467
36:56.425 --> 36:59.185
Thanks. You too.

468
37:00.545 --> 37:02.425
I liked your guitar sound in the last round.

469
37:02.505 --> 37:05.945
Me too. I liked your rearrangement.

470
37:06.545 --> 37:09.785
I'm going all out in the final round.

471
37:10.385 --> 37:12.905
Same here. There's no way I'll lose to you.

472
37:25.345 --> 37:29.385
I MIGHT BE UNLUCKY

473
37:41.825 --> 37:43.465
You've been working hard since early morning.

474
37:46.985 --> 37:50.105
I want to finish writing the song so we have time to practice with our band.

475
37:51.625 --> 37:53.905
Don't you have an exam today?

476
37:53.985 --> 37:55.145
I bought you congee.

477
37:55.225 --> 37:56.985
Eat quickly, then go take your exam.

478
37:57.665 --> 38:00.385
Thanks. Have you eaten?

479
38:00.465 --> 38:02.665
Take a break and eat congee with me, okay?

480
38:03.545 --> 38:04.865
I'll get it ready.

481
38:06.865 --> 38:10.545
Hey, are you okay?

482
38:11.145 --> 38:13.465
You're burning up.

483
38:13.545 --> 38:14.585
Hey.

484
38:17.025 --> 38:18.505
You should get some rest.

485
39:10.705 --> 39:11.705
I'm full.

486
39:13.705 --> 39:14.785
Then…

487
39:17.425 --> 39:18.705
Take some medicine.

488
39:18.785 --> 39:20.305
No.

489
39:20.385 --> 39:22.185
I said take it.

490
39:22.785 --> 39:23.905
No.

491
39:23.985 --> 39:26.625
You have to. Here.

492
39:40.545 --> 39:43.305
All right. Now go get some sleep.

493
39:45.625 --> 39:47.705
But I haven't finished the song.

494
39:48.305 --> 39:52.105
Hey, rest first.

495
39:52.705 --> 39:54.705
Sleep. Trust me.

496
40:19.185 --> 40:20.905
Once the curse is lifted,

497
40:20.985 --> 40:25.225
the cursed person will lose all memories of the curser,

498
40:25.305 --> 40:27.585
as if they never knew each other.

499
40:38.865 --> 40:41.345
Did Khobfa forget to water you?

500
40:41.905 --> 40:43.905
You're wilting just like your owner.

501
40:47.665 --> 40:52.585
Sorry, but he's focused on his band right now.

502
40:59.065 --> 41:00.665
Hello? What's up?

503
41:00.745 --> 41:02.785
Rin, where are you?

504
41:02.865 --> 41:05.465
There's a graded body-painting exam today.

505
41:05.545 --> 41:07.865
The professor called your name three times.

506
41:07.945 --> 41:08.905
Did you forget?

507
41:08.985 --> 41:10.625
I didn't forget.

508
41:10.705 --> 41:12.065
I probably can't make it.

509
41:12.145 --> 41:15.065
Khobfa is sick, so I have to stay with him.

510
41:15.665 --> 41:16.785
Go take your exam.

511
41:18.305 --> 41:19.465
I'm fine.

512
41:20.065 --> 41:22.025
I don't want you to fail an exam because of me.

513
41:24.585 --> 41:28.625
Ohm, I'm taking leave today. Please tell the professor. Bye.

514
41:30.265 --> 41:32.785
You're usually serious about grades, right?

515
41:35.505 --> 41:37.945
But you're the most important thing right now.

516
41:47.505 --> 41:50.065
I've decided. It's okay.

517
41:50.625 --> 41:52.065
Go back to sleep.

518
41:57.625 --> 41:58.945
I'll give you five minutes.

519
42:01.705 --> 42:02.705
For what?

520
42:06.825 --> 42:09.065
I'm sorry. I was talking to a customer for so long.

521
42:09.145 --> 42:10.305
Come on. Let's eat.

522
42:12.105 --> 42:12.985
What are you doing?

523
42:13.065 --> 42:16.625
Wait. Turn around first.

524
42:17.385 --> 42:18.705
Yeah, turn around.

525
42:21.665 --> 42:22.665
What are you doing?

526
42:22.745 --> 42:24.345
Just a second.

527
42:29.705 --> 42:30.705
Turn around.

528
42:33.185 --> 42:34.065
Surprise!

529
42:34.145 --> 42:35.385
What do you think?

530
42:35.985 --> 42:37.585
I made this for you.

531
42:37.665 --> 42:39.025
Wow.

532
42:39.105 --> 42:40.625
Come sit down.

533
42:41.705 --> 42:43.305
Hurry.

534
42:46.745 --> 42:51.465
I may not have much money, but this is what I can do right now.

535
42:52.105 --> 42:55.745
When I win the prize money,

536
42:56.865 --> 42:58.905
I'll treat you to a special meal.

537
43:00.265 --> 43:02.025
This is already very special.

538
43:03.865 --> 43:04.785
What?

539
43:05.425 --> 43:07.065
Nothing. Let me taste it.

540
43:07.145 --> 43:09.425
Wait.

541
43:11.025 --> 43:12.305
I'll feed you.

542
43:14.905 --> 43:16.025
Open wide.

543
43:22.905 --> 43:24.745
How is it? Is it okay?

544
43:33.145 --> 43:34.265
Better than I expected.

545
43:34.345 --> 43:35.265
Are you lying?

546
43:35.345 --> 43:36.625
No, really. Taste it.

547
43:54.185 --> 43:55.945
Khobfa, enough.

548
43:56.025 --> 43:57.945
My professor is strict. He won't listen to you.

549
43:58.025 --> 44:01.265
No. I caused you trouble, so I have to take responsibility.

550
44:01.345 --> 44:03.065
No need.

551
44:04.345 --> 44:05.505
I'll handle it.

552
44:12.545 --> 44:13.825
Hello, Professor.

553
44:13.905 --> 44:15.305
Hello, Professor.

554
44:15.825 --> 44:19.265
I'm really sorry Rin missed the exam.

555
44:19.345 --> 44:20.385
It was because of me.

556
44:20.465 --> 44:22.585
He had to stay and take care of me.

557
44:22.665 --> 44:24.385
Please don't deduct Rin's grades.

558
44:26.985 --> 44:28.385
Rules are rules.

559
44:28.465 --> 44:30.145
You missed the body-painting exam.

560
44:30.225 --> 44:33.905
It's worth 30 points, Rin. Understand?

561
44:33.985 --> 44:34.945
Yes, Professor.

562
44:35.025 --> 44:36.265
But the time isn't up yet, right?

563
44:37.465 --> 44:40.025
The other students just finished early, correct?

564
44:40.745 --> 44:45.385
I'm sorry. I called Ohm and Jinnie.

565
44:46.745 --> 44:50.505
You're right. You have 90 minutes left.

566
44:50.585 --> 44:52.305
Can you finish in time, Rin?

567
44:52.905 --> 44:54.705
-Ninety minutes, Professor? -Yes.

568
44:56.025 --> 44:57.985
Where am I going to find a model?

569
44:58.065 --> 44:59.585
I already gave up my booking.

570
45:06.465 --> 45:10.505
I'm sorry. Am I the only one who doesn't know what's going on?

571
45:16.185 --> 45:17.265
Come here.

572
45:36.945 --> 45:39.745
Easy. Take it slow.

573
45:40.505 --> 45:41.825
Don't worry.

574
45:42.505 --> 45:43.745
Idiot!

575
45:45.985 --> 45:46.905
You can do it.

576
46:44.425 --> 46:49.585
I might be unlucky

577
46:50.185 --> 46:54.985
As if I'm cursed with bad luck

578
46:56.305 --> 46:57.305
Hey!

579
46:58.265 --> 47:00.665
I just thought of the melody for our new song.

580
47:00.745 --> 47:02.185
Keep painting.

581
47:05.705 --> 47:10.585
I might be unlucky

582
47:12.105 --> 47:16.905
As if I'm cursed with bad luck

583
47:18.145 --> 47:21.305
Whatever I do, I end up hurt

584
47:21.905 --> 47:25.385
Disappointed in everything

585
47:26.425 --> 47:30.665
Yet there is one lucky thing

586
47:31.185 --> 47:35.745
Whatever happens, you are always there

587
47:36.425 --> 47:40.145
No matter how unlucky I am

588
47:40.225 --> 47:43.065
I'm lucky

589
47:44.665 --> 47:48.745
Just to have you in my life

590
47:53.425 --> 47:55.825
How is it? Do you like it?

591
47:58.145 --> 47:59.145
Yeah.

592
48:00.545 --> 48:02.145
I love it.

593
48:02.225 --> 48:05.145
I secretly put our story into the song too.

594
48:06.105 --> 48:09.945
Yet there is one lucky thing

595
48:10.025 --> 48:14.105
Whatever happens, you are always there

596
48:14.185 --> 48:16.705
No matter how unlucky I am

597
48:16.785 --> 48:20.225
I'm lucky

598
48:20.305 --> 48:25.625
Just to have you in my life

599
48:38.145 --> 48:39.905
I wouldn't call this decent.

600
48:43.145 --> 48:46.825
It's outstanding. An A for sure.

601
48:46.905 --> 48:48.265
A D wouldn't do it justice.

602
48:49.905 --> 48:52.185
-Thank you, Professor. -Thank you.

603
48:53.465 --> 48:56.465
Pack up, clean yourself up, and go home.

604
48:56.545 --> 48:57.425
-Yes. -Okay.

605
48:59.305 --> 49:03.065
Damn. It's A-level work.

606
49:03.145 --> 49:04.345
Let me take some photos.

607
49:04.425 --> 49:05.265
Come on.

608
49:05.985 --> 49:08.625
Whoa, look.

609
49:09.305 --> 49:11.025
I don't think you need to shower tonight.

610
49:11.625 --> 49:12.745
Great job.

611
49:22.305 --> 49:23.665
What should we do?

612
49:23.745 --> 49:25.145
It won't wash off.

613
49:28.705 --> 49:31.265
Just leave it. It's fine.

614
49:31.345 --> 49:34.945
But if you leave it, you'll stay stained.

615
49:35.025 --> 49:36.145
Is that okay?

616
49:36.745 --> 49:38.625
It's fine.

617
49:38.705 --> 49:43.265
It'll be a trace of our good memories. Isn't that nice?

618
49:51.185 --> 49:52.505
Is this spot done yet?

619
50:11.465 --> 50:12.865
Can I kiss you?

620
50:14.105 --> 50:14.945
What?

621
50:15.025 --> 50:17.385
Are you going to kiss me to prove true love again?

622
50:17.465 --> 50:19.025
This isn't Rayong.

623
50:19.625 --> 50:21.865
Please. Just once.

624
50:21.945 --> 50:22.825
Please.

625
50:25.025 --> 50:26.545
But…

626
50:26.625 --> 50:29.305
Think of it as my reward for talking to the professor for you.

627
50:29.385 --> 50:32.665
Wow, now you're holding that over me.

628
50:33.745 --> 50:35.705
So? Will you allow me to?

629
50:35.785 --> 50:38.065
If you take too long, I'll take two.

630
50:41.545 --> 50:42.945
Fine.

631
52:07.825 --> 52:09.505
Would it be too selfish of me?

632
52:13.625 --> 52:16.025
THE CURSED PERSON WILL LOSE ALL MEMORIES OF THE CURSER,

633
52:16.105 --> 52:17.745
AS IF THEY NEVER KNEW EACH OTHER.

634
52:19.905 --> 52:21.425
Rin, I'm done.

635
52:28.945 --> 52:30.865
Come on. Let's go back to the room.

636
52:40.265 --> 52:41.385
I'll tie it for you.

637
52:45.945 --> 52:47.865
I'm sorry, Khobfa.

638
52:48.825 --> 52:50.385
I just want to…

639
52:52.025 --> 52:54.105
stay in your memories a little longer.

640
53:12.385 --> 53:13.745
Our band is getting in sync.

641
53:13.825 --> 53:16.705
If this keeps up, we'll do great in the final round.

642
53:16.785 --> 53:19.305
Thank you for always believing in me.

643
53:19.385 --> 53:20.865
During the final rehearsal and the final,

644
53:20.945 --> 53:23.105
I'm going to surprise Rin and ask him to be my boyfriend.

645
53:23.185 --> 53:25.305
What? You're going to ask Rin out?

646
53:25.385 --> 53:26.705
Just open your heart.

647
53:27.305 --> 53:28.425
I'm waiting for you.

648
53:29.105 --> 53:30.625
Or should I lift the curse?

649
53:30.705 --> 53:33.825
But if you don't, Khobfa will be unlucky forever.

650
53:34.425 --> 53:37.385
Would you take someone unlucky as your boyfriend?

651
53:37.465 --> 53:40.145
-Date him! -Date him!

652
53:40.225 --> 53:42.305
BE MY BOYFRIEND
